{
  "_header": "Captured rows 1-32 of playtest session 0106e608-e5f0-4ff9-89e2-16f780dbc002 (docs/playtests/2026-11-13-r1-spine-test-drive.md findings 4 and 7), read-only from vm-104 stacks-dev-db-1 on 2026-11-13. The human user id is replaced by PLAYER_USER. Rows 21, 22 and 30 hold the shipped text. `react` holds the raw talk-turn react outputs (seq 21 job 32112a98, seq 30 job e5eb04d1, speaker wenna). `correctedSeq21` is the seq 21 text with the Snag sentence removed. Spec 112 plan D6 and D7.",
  "sessionId": "0106e608-e5f0-4ff9-89e2-16f780dbc002",
  "react": {
    "seq21": {
      "speaker": "wenna",
      "text": "A voice cracks low from the ferry-house shadow, counting under breath — three, three, three — before Wenna Marsh steps into view, knuckles white on a boat-hook. \"Who's walkin' my bank at dusk,\" she rasps, eyes darting to the cut rope swinging above. \"Pell's not back. Snag's not back. You seen either, or you just come to gawk at an old woman's trouble?\""
    },
    "seq30": {
      "speaker": "wenna",
      "text": "Last I seen 'em — reeds past the bend, three days gone. Pell went for eel-traps, Snag followed grumblin'. Neither come back for supper, nor the one after. Water's loud there, swallows sound. I counted the hours — three, nine, twenty-seven — till I quit countin' and come lookin' myself. Found the rope cut 'fore I found them."
    }
  },
