    {
      "sessionId": "0106e608-e5f0-4ff9-89e2-16f780dbc002",
      "seq": 21,
      "actor": "ai:dm",
      "type": "narration",
      "payload": {
        "text": "A voice cracks low from the ferry-house shadow, counting under breath — three, three, three — before Wenna Marsh steps into view, knuckles white on a boat-hook. \"Who's walkin' my bank at dusk,\" she rasps, eyes darting to the cut rope swinging above. \"Pell's not back. Snag's not back. You seen either, or you just come to gawk at an old woman's trouble?\"",
        "actionIds": []
      },
      "payloadVersion": 1,
      "visibility": "public",
      "ts": "2026-11-14T02:12:13.224605+00:00"
    },
    {
      "sessionId": "0106e608-e5f0-4ff9-89e2-16f780dbc002",
      "seq": 22,
      "actor": "ai:companion:odo",
      "type": "talk",
      "payload": {
        "text": "Peace, goodwife, peace. We're no gawkers — we've come to see the ferry sing again. Pell and Snag, you say? A cut rope rarely cuts itself. Tell us where you last saw them, and we'll walk that bank with you.",
        "channel": "ic",
        "characterId": "odo"
      },
      "payloadVersion": 1,
      "visibility": "public",
      "ts": "2026-11-14T02:12:17.614557+00:00"
    },
    {
      "sessionId": "0106e608-e5f0-4ff9-89e2-16f780dbc002",
      "seq": 23,
      "actor": "ai:companion:kestrel",
      "type": "talk",
      "payload": {
        "text": "Sawn clean means someone wanted that bell silent, not broken — worth remembering.",
        "channel": "ic",
        "characterId": "kestrel"
      },
      "payloadVersion": 1,
      "visibility": "public",
      "ts": "2026-11-14T02:12:19.79326+00:00"
    },
    {
      "sessionId": "0106e608-e5f0-4ff9-89e2-16f780dbc002",
      "seq": 24,
      "actor": "ai:dm",
      "type": "journal.entry.added",
      "payload": {
        "body": "At the bank near the ferry-house, Tamsin Vale explored the area as dusk approached. Wenna Marsh, the ferry-house keeper, emerged from the shadows counting to herself. She confronted the party with a boat-hook in hand, her knuckles white with tension. She revealed that both Pell and Snag—presumably crew members—have not returned, and she gestured to a cut rope hanging above, suggesting the ferry bell has been deliberately silenced. Wenna demanded to know if the party had seen either man or were simply come to witness her trouble.",
        "title": "The ferry-house keeper's distress at Greyhollow Ford",
        "entryId": "chron-0106e608-21",
        "sourceActionIds": ["18", "21"]
      },
      "payloadVersion": 1,
      "visibility": "public",
      "ts": "2026-11-14T02:12:21.853686+00:00"
